data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","output_index":0,"item_id":"rs_090aca0ffaaa6de7016afda8f7e62c87d1a40331f8b50ce8b6","summary_index":0,"text":"**Calculating multiples and odd counts**\n\nI need to calculate the multiples below 100 for 1 to 99. For multiples of 3, I find 33. For multiples of 7, it’s 14. When I consider both, the overlap for multiples of 21 gives me 4. Now, using XOR logic, I get an odd count of 39. Once I finish that, I’ll check the weather in Lima, and I’ll be sure to use the tool one at a time!","sequence_number":91}

